From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominik Krivohlavek <github@xkrivo.net>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:19:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 22/28] fix(midea): log unknown floor materials at debug level

The firmware accepts floor materials 0-4, but only 0, 2 and 3 have known
names. The segment rendering already falls back to generic for the other
values; the room info parser however logged a warning every time it saw
one. Log it at debug level instead.

Materials 1 and 4 remain unnamed; their meaning is unknown.

diff --git a/backend/lib/robots/midea/MideaMapParser.js b/backend/lib/robots/midea/MideaMapParser.js
index 460a5772..bcab8484 100644
--- a/backend/lib/robots/midea/MideaMapParser.js
+++ b/backend/lib/robots/midea/MideaMapParser.js
@@ -880,7 +880,7 @@ class MideaMapParser {
 
             const mappedMaterial = FLOOR_MATERIAL_MAPPING[material];
             if (!mappedMaterial) {
-                Logger.warn(`Encountered unknown material '${material}' for segment '${roomId}'`);
+                Logger.debug(`Encountered unknown material '${material}' for segment '${roomId}', treating as generic`);
             }
 
             offset += 10;
